9: //! channel rather than written to the socket directly. The supervisor drains
10: //! the queue onto whatever connection is currently live; while disconnected,
11: //! queued messages are dropped. This means callers never observe a "broken
12: //! pipe" — sending always succeeds locally and delivery resumes after reconnect.
